      "ownership": "unknown"
    },
    "parts": [
      {
        "part_label": "(a)",
        "part_text": "Parathyroid hormone (PTH) - The parathyroid hormone is secreted by the parathyroid gland. Its main function is to increase the level of calcium in blood. It promotes the reabsorption of calcium from nephrons and also, promotes the absorption of calcium from digested food. Hence, it plays an important role in maintaining calcium balance in the body.",
        "part_latex": null,
        "answer_text": "The parathyroid hormone increases blood calcium levels and promotes calcium reabsorption.",
        "answer_latex": null,
        "steps": [],
        "final_answer": "Therefore, PTH is crucial for calcium homeostasis.",
        "answer_image": {
          "present": false,
          "description": null,
          "cloudinary_url": null,
          "latex_extracted": null,
          "source_page_number": null,
          "source_image_index": null,
          "ownership": "unknown"
        },
        "question_images": [],
        "answer_images": [],
        "question_image": {
          "present": false,
          "description": null,
          "cloudinary_url": null,
          "latex_extracted": null,
          "source_page_number": null,
          "source_image_index": null,
          "ownership": "unknown"
        }
      },
      {
        "part_label": "(b)",
        "part_text": "Thyroid hormones - Thyroid hormones such as thyroxine, triiodothyronin, and thyrocalcitonin are secreted by the thyroid gland. Thyroxine maintains the basal metabolic rate of the body and regulates the carbohydrate, fat, and protein metabolism. Water and electrolyte balance is also maintained by thyroid hormones. Thyrocalcitonin or calcitonin lowers calcium level in blood plasma. It plays a significant role in calcium levels along with parathyroid hormone.",
        "part_latex": null,
        "answer_text": "Thyroid hormones regulate metabolism and maintain calcium levels.",
        "answer_latex": null,
        "steps": [],
        "final_answer": "Thus, they are essential for metabolic regulation.",
        "answer_image": {
          "present": false,
          "description": null,
          "cloudinary_url": null,
          "latex_extracted": null,
          "source_page_number": null,
          "source_image_index": null,
          "ownership": "unknown"
        },
        "question_images": [],
        "answer_images": [],
        "question_image": {
          "present": false,
          "description": null,
          "cloudinary_url": null,
          "latex_extracted": null,
          "source_page_number": null,
          "source_image_index": null,
          "ownership": "unknown"
        }
      },
      {
        "part_label": "(c)",
        "part_text": "Thymosins - Thymosin is secreted by the thymus gland. It plays a major role in protecting the body against infectious agents. It helps in the differentiation of T-lymphocytes and also promotes the reproduction of antibodies. Hence, it provides both cell-mediated and humoral immunity. Thymosins also help in the development of sex glands.",
        "part_latex": null,
        "answer_text": "Thymosins are crucial for immune response and T-cell differentiation.",
        "answer_latex": null,
        "steps": [],
        "final_answer": "Therefore, they are vital for adaptive immunity.",
        "answer_image": {
          "present": false,
          "description": null,
          "cloudinary_url": null,
          "latex_extracted": null,
          "source_page_number": null,
          "source_image_index": null,
          "ownership": "unknown"
        },
        "question_images": [],
        "answer_images": [],
        "question_image": {
          "present": false,
          "description": null,
          "cloudinary_url": null,
          "latex_extracted": null,
          "source_page_number": null,
          "source_image_index": null,
          "ownership": "unknown"
        }
      },
      {
        "part_label": "(d)",
        "part_text": "Androgens - The leydig cells of testis produce androgens such as testosterone. Testosterone is a male sex hormone that regulates the development of secondary sex characteristics such as facial hair, hoarse voice, development of reproductive organ, etc. Androgens also regulate the development, maturation, and functions of various male accessory organs such as epididymis and prostate glands. It stimulates spermatogenesis and formation of mature sperms. It also influences male sexual behaviour.",
        "part_latex": null,
        "answer_text": "Androgens regulate male secondary sexual characteristics and spermatogenesis.",
        "answer_latex": null,
        "steps": [],
        "final_answer": "Thus, they are essential for male reproductive health.",
        "answer_image": {
          "present": false,
          "description": null,
          "cloudinary_url": null,
          "latex_extracted": null,
          "source_page_number": null,
          "source_image_index": null,
