          "source_page_number": null,
          "source_image_index": null,
          "ownership": "unknown"
        }
      },
      {
        "part_label": "(e)",
        "part_text": "Estrogens - Estrogen is the female sex hormone that controls the development of secondary sex characteristics such as enlargement of breasts and development of female reproductive organs. It plays a role in the development, growth and maturation of female secondary characteristics. It also helps in the development of growing ovarian follicles. It influences female sexual behaviour.",
        "part_latex": null,
        "answer_text": "Estrogens are responsible for female secondary sexual characteristics and reproductive health.",
        "answer_latex": null,
        "steps": [],
        "final_answer": "Therefore, they are crucial for female reproductive functions.",
        "answer_image": {
          "present": false,
          "description": null,
